## Experiment 1: Flutter and Dart Setup

In this experiment, the Flutter and Dart development environment was configured for the Food Ordering App. Flutter is used to develop the application interface, while Dart is used as the programming language. The development environment was prepared using Flutter SDK, Dart SDK, Android Studio or Visual Studio Code, Android SDK, emulator, and Git.

The Flutter project was created and tested using basic Flutter commands. The `flutter doctor` command was used to check whether the required development tools and dependencies were properly configured. The project was then executed using `flutter run` to verify that the application was working correctly.

Basic Dart programming concepts were also explored, including variables, data types, arithmetic operations, functions, and conditional statements. These concepts provide the programming foundation required for developing different features of the Food Ordering App.

The main purpose of this experiment was to establish a working Flutter environment and understand the basics of Dart programming before starting the application development. After completing the setup, the project was ready for further development of the restaurant list, food menu, cart, order form, and order status features.

